For the CLI I want to build it with .NET. Only reason being is because i'm well versed in the stack and I don't want the overhead with trying to learn a new stack for building this CLI.

This CLI will be used by an admin (ME) and will not be user facing. The main purpose is to:

- CREATE/READ/UPDATE/DELETE playable streams
- view analystics

The general pipeline is as follows:

1. admin uploads audio
2. cli then uploads it to our service that generates/stores blobs
3. that service gives us the protected blob url and also the playable stream
4. we then insert it into the DB

We are going to use Backblaze as the blob storage, but currently they do not have a .NET SDK so we'll use their prescribed method of using the AWS SDK. Please double check backblaze docs on this.

Here's the arguements i'm thinking of:

--file or -f "some local file"
--title or -t "title of the file"
--published or -p "publish or not"
